## What I'm building

An AI cold-calling system for a Final Expense (burial life insurance) campaign in the US, plus the CRM around it. An AI bot dials leads, qualifies them, and transfers live calls to a human verifier, who then hands off to a licensed agent who closes the sale.

I'm a small business owner, not an engineer. I use Claude Code in VS Code on my office Windows PC to build, and I speak Roman Urdu. Please reply in Roman Urdu.

## The shape of the system

1. **Retell AI** (cloud) — holds the voice agent "Sarah" and places the calls. Agent ID `agent_1106515681f404064d0d5c008e`, workspace "Smart". Single-prompt agent, Kate voice, voicemail detection with hang-up, IVR hangup on, `end_call` and `transfer_call` configured. Model is currently Claude 5 Sonnet at ~$0.152/min; GPT-4.1 (~$0.13/min all-in) is worth testing as a cheaper swap.
2. **My app** — a local web app doing everything else: leads, compliance, dialer, webhook receiver, CRM, verifier and closer workspaces, recordings, transcripts, analytics, spend. Node + Fastify + React + SQLite, encrypted PII.
3. **The people** — verifiers take the bot's transfers; licensed agents (closers) take the verifier's handoffs and record the outcome.

