## What is built and working

Leads, compliance (federal DNC, internal DNC, per-state hours, unbypassable `scrub()` gate), the dialer, the webhook (signature-verified, idempotent), verifier workspace (16-question checklist), closer workspace (My Queue, atomic claim lock, appointed states, auto-release), sessions scoped per user, dashboard, analytics (contact rate by hour, caller ID health, speed to lead, CPA by vendor), server-side recordings, live websocket updates.

Added since the last handoff:
- **Recording consent by state** and **data retention** with split windows, legal holds, purge log, per-customer file.
- **Call transcripts (bot leg)** — stored, shown speaker by speaker in the CRM, downloadable, admin-only bulk export with personal data redacted by default and logged. Per-state transcript policy (store / store-and-flag / do-not-store), every state defaulting to store-and-flag marked "unreviewed — awaiting attorney". A transcript is only stored if the recording disclosure was delivered. Changing a setting never clears the unreviewed flag; only an explicit "reviewed with attorney" does.
- **TCPA litigator gate** — the check existed but answered "clean" against an empty list, which is a control that reports a pass without running. Now it says "no litigator list loaded" plainly, and going live is blocked unless a list is loaded or an admin types a confirmation, audit-logged.
- **Licence expiry** per state, warnings and claim blocking.
- **Transfer failure handling** — an unclaimed transfer is released after 8 minutes, a callback booked through `scrub()`, idempotent so one customer can't collect a hundred callbacks.
- **Ownership fix** — reproduced a real bug: admin and licensed agent could both write to the same session and the admin's save silently overwrote the person actually on the phone. Now the current owner is the only one who can edit; everyone else gets a live view-only notice, enforced server-side, and unsaved admin text is preserved rather than saved over.
- **Spend tracking** — Retell sends the real per-call cost, so spend is actual, not estimated. Retell publishes no balance API, so I record top-ups manually and the app shows "estimated remaining", clearly labelled. No per-agent cost breakdown (most calls never reach an agent). Twilio live balance is supported for later.
- **Backups**, auto-start via a Scheduled Task at logon (commands written, not run), health check now asserts the UI is served, test isolation hardened so tests can never touch the real database, and a test-cleanup bug fixed that had left 1,053 folders and 3.1 GB behind.

## Decisions already made — please don't reverse these without asking

- Re-pooling leads **grants** extra attempts, never resets `attempts_count`.
- Nothing bypasses `scrub()` — no bulk action, no callback, no manual dial, and no phone feature.
- Whoever currently owns a call is the only one who can edit it; everyone else, including admins, is view-only.
- Rates are never computed from samples too small to mean anything; users are compared against the team median, never ranked.
- The app never shows a balance it cannot verify; an estimate is labelled as an estimate.
- Depth over coverage on compliance work — a thin version is worse than none.
- Every prompt to Claude Code must end with an instruction to test and verify in the real browser and reconcile on-screen numbers against the database.
- Claude Code cannot reach the laptop, my phone, or the Retell dashboard. Anything there is MANUAL TEST REQUIRED, never claimed as passing.

## In progress — the phone layer (option C)

The CRM was always meant to be where verifiers work. So the phone is being built **inside the CRM** using **Twilio**, not a per-user phone service (CloudTalk and 3CX were priced and rejected — the difference was about one policy a month).

Design: Retell transfers to my Twilio number, the call queues, it rings whichever verifier is available in the CRM, the customer's record opens automatically linked to that call, the verifier can transfer to a licensed agent and stay on or leave, and the human legs are recorded into the existing retention, legal hold and consent rules. Dialer pacing stops the bot transferring more calls than there are free verifiers. Hold limit 2 minutes with hold music, never silence. Verifier-stage editing limited to the verifier who claimed the call.

Phase 0: 2–3 days. Phase 1 (the usable version): 3–4 weeks. Phase 2 (SIP transfers, reconnect, supervisor listen-in, removing the unused VICIdial code): 2–3 weeks. Being built in small working slices, each fully tested before the next: (1) verifier receives a call in the browser, (2) call auto-linked to the customer, (3) routing to whoever is free with hold and callback, (4) transfer to agent with stay/leave, (5) human-leg recording, (6) dialer pacing.

Plan lives in `docs/PHONE_OPTION_C.md`.

