## Economics, corrected

**A closed policy earns about $110, not $500–1,000.** That changes everything downstream:

- Retell at 400 dials/day: roughly $465–815/month depending on the model.
- Twilio phone layer: small by comparison.
- **Leads dominate.** 400 dials/day at ~3 attempts per lead is ~2,900 fresh leads/month. At $10 each that's ~$29,000/month and a break-even nearer 270 policies/month. My real lead cost and my leads-per-policy rate are the numbers that decide whether this campaign works — everything else is noise beside them.

I raised scraping my own leads to avoid this cost. I was advised against it: scraped data carries no consent, AI-voice calls need prior express written consent, penalties run $500–1,500 per call, and this industry has lawyers who look for exactly this. Legitimate cheaper routes: shared or aged leads (consent proof still required), bulk negotiation, or my own lead generation where I control the consent wording.

## Legal framing I've already been told

AI-voice calls fall under the TCPA's rules for artificial/prerecorded voices, so they need prior express written consent for cell numbers, and consent given to a lead generator generally doesn't transfer to me. Purchased and aged lists are the risky case. I need documented consent per lead, monthly DNC refreshes, and an attorney's review before running a real campaign. Claude is not my lawyer and should keep saying so.
